nnexj.pdf</ext-link> [accessed 6 April 2007].</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b23-ehp0115-a00238"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><collab>WHO</collab> 2005a. Health Effects of the Chernobyl Accident and Special Health Care Programmes. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/entity/ionizing_radiation/a_e/chernobyl/-EGH%20Master%20file%202005.08.24.pdf">http://www.who.int/entity/ionizing_radiation/a_e/chernobyl/-EGH%20Master%20file%202005.08.24.pdf</ext-link> [accessed 20 September 2006]</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b24-ehp0115-a00238"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><collab>WHO</collab> 2005b. Chernobyl: The True Scale of the Accident: 20 Years Later a UN Report Provides Definitive Answers and Ways to Repair Lives. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/mediacentre/news/releases/2005/pr38/en/index.html">http://www.who.int/mediacentre/news/releases/2005/pr38/en/index.html</ext-link> [accessed 6 April 2007].</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b25-ehp0115-a00238"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Whyte</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>First day neonatal mortality since 1935: reexamination of the Cross hypothesis</article-title><source>BMJ</source><volume>304</volume><fpage>343</fpage><lpage>346</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1540730</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>